From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:33:17 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] klatt::synth: keep the stress lookahead within the elements

The lookahead for the next stressed element read a duration past the end of the elements when it reached it. darray's zero-filled spare usually held it, but an element array that filled its allocation read past the heap block. The duration past the end is now 0, as the spare gave.
---
 src/audiosource/speech/klatt.cpp | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/audiosource/speech/klatt.cpp b/src/audiosource/speech/klatt.cpp
index c9572f0..0ab2bfa 100644
--- a/src/audiosource/speech/klatt.cpp
+++ b/src/audiosource/speech/klatt.cpp
@@ -984,7 +984,7 @@ int klatt::synth(int /* aSampleCount */, short *aSamplePointer)
 						{
 							d += du;
 							e = (j < mElementCount) ? &gElement[mElement[j++]] : &gElement[0];
-							du = mElement[j++];
+							du = (j < mElementCount) ? mElement[j++] : 0;
 						}
 
 						while ((e->mFeat & ELM_FEATURE_VWL) && mElement[j++] == s);
